<attribute name="name" nodeId="4e14fa0f">Define the control structure for the program</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="5d86b1aa">_MQBUkMarEeSZS6zUrl8OeQ</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="1fec3aa4">Define the control structure for the program</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="4e3688d9"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="1c783f5">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="876d6133"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="b5c65f9e">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="453e12dd"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="6d4c7e82">&lt;p&gt;
    Confirm the executive sponsor, program sponsor, program manager, and other key members&lt;br /&gt;
    of the program management and control structure.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    To facilitate program communications and decision-making, there should be one program&lt;br /&gt;
    sponsor and one program manager for the program.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The program sponsor should be a manager in the appropriate area of the business. The&lt;br /&gt;
    specific managerial level of this person should correspond with the importance and visibility&lt;br /&gt;
    of the program.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The program manager should possess the relevant skills and experience to successfully&lt;br /&gt;
    manage the program and, if possible, should be familiar with the enterprise&apos;s business or a&lt;br /&gt;
    similar business.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Define any other review groups or individuals who will be involved in managing the&lt;br /&gt;
    program.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    If the enterprise has an existing management and control structure, map the methodology&lt;br /&gt;
    roles to it.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
